{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall go outside the camp.</b> Scripture teaches you: a pure priest who may enter the camp — he purifies the metzora, for it is written 'and he shall go out'; and if he did not enter the camp, how would he go out from it? But an impure priest who may not enter the camp does not purify the metzora. And behold, he is healed, that the plague departed." "<b>Plague.</b> That departed — white hair. <b>The tzara'at.</b> That departed — the living skin. מן הצרוע — even partial white hair."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:06.963402446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}